After glBindFrameBuffer, you can either glClear or not. Not doing a clear will load the contents of the attachments from memory.

After doing a sequence of draw operations on FB, you could call glInvalidateFramebuffer to indicate the data is transient i.e., keep color but trash depth/stencil

Similar to Metal Load/Store actions for Color, Depth and Stencil buffers

----
glBindFrameBuffer(FB0)
glClear(...)
glDraw(...)
glInvalidateFramebuffer()

glBindFramebuffer(FB1)
// Use FB0 as texture
glClear()
glDraw()
swapBuffers()

